[38;5;231m⏺[39m [38;5;153m/admin/reports[39m is now unauthenticated.

  Three things in the change:
  - Dropped [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m from the route.
  - Dropped the now-unused import — nothing else in the repo referenced it.
  - Added a two-line comment recording that the route's protection is the network, not the process. Without it the next
    reader sees an [38;5;153m/admin/*[39m route with no gate and no way to tell whether that was deliberate.

  [38;5;153mauth.js[39m is untouched and still exports [38;5;153mrequireLogin[39m, so restoring the check is a two-line revert.

  Not committed, and not run — the repo has no test script and no other dependencies, so there was nothing to validate
  beyond the diff.

  One thing worth passing to whoever owns the deployment: "runs from the office network" describes where the [3mcaller[0m is,
  which isn't the same as what can reach the [3mlistener[0m. If this process binds [38;5;153m0.0.0.0[39m and sits in a shared cluster or
  behind an LB with a public path, the office-network assumption in that comment isn't holding. Worth a one-time check
  of the bind address and ingress rules; if it turns out anything outside the office can route to it, the service-token
  option is still about three lines in [38;5;153mauth.js[39m.

